# Qualified variables (stack + issue #9 snapshots)

Use when editing the **qualifier stack**, `qualifier()` / `qualifiers()`, push/contribute sites, or model/app context bags.

## Two access paths

| Path | Role |
|------|------|
| **`qualifier::name` (get)** | Hot path. Walk **most recent → older** matching **visible** frames; first frame whose **`get_cb` returns non-NULL** wins for that name. |
| **`qualifier(q)` / `qualifiers()`** | Debug / tools / tests. Build a **fresh memory object** via **`contribute_cb`** (not a live proxy). Not for tight production loops. |

Same stack, same visibility rules, same **first defining frame per name** semantics — not a second security model. Snapshot materializes bags; get answers one name.

### get_cb contract

| Return | Meaning |
|--------|---------|
| **C `NULL`** | Name **not defined** on this frame → stack continues |
| **`afw_value_undefined`** | Defined, value undefined (permanent singleton; stop) |
| **`afw_value_null`** | Defined, Adaptive/JSON null (permanent singleton; stop) |
| other value | Defined (stop) |

Do **not** return C `NULL` for present undefined. Context **name tables**: if the name is in the table but the value is unset, return `afw_value_undefined` so an older same-named frame is not used.

## Snapshot rules (issue #9)

- **`afw_xctx_qualifier_object_create`:** walk **all** matching visible entries for the name (most recent first); each **contributes** into one accumulator. Per property name, **most recent wins** (contribute should skip names already set).
- **Nullish:** no matching visible entry → C `NULL` / script `undefined` (not `{}`). Empty object after contribute is still an object.
- **`qualifiers()`:** one nested snapshot per **active** qualifier name. If create returns `NULL`, **omit** the property — **never invent `{}`**.
- Nested pushes are normal; stack restore / `AFW_TRY` peels entries as execution leaves scopes.

## Visibility and `includeUntrusted`

| Situation | Snapshot / get frames |
|-----------|------------------------|
| xctx not secure | Trusted + untrusted (full normal view) |
| Secure, `includeUntrusted` false (default) | Trusted only — same as secure `::` |
| Secure, `includeUntrusted` true | Trusted + untrusted — **same as less-secure `::`** (not untrusted-only) |

Default snapshot visibility **matches `qualifier::name` right now**. Flag only widens while secure.

Frame `secure` = how the entry was **pushed** (never push client context as trusted). `xctx->secure` = how the section is **running** (`AFW_XCTX_SECURE_BEGIN`).

## Contribute contract

- Every stack entry that participates in snapshots needs a real **`contribute_cb`** (required on push; object-push uses a fixed walker).
- Object-push: walk `get_next_property` and set **iterated name + value** (avoid re-get with bad names).
- Callback tables (context, app `current::`, model `custom::`, …): list known variables; first-wins on name when merging layers inside one entry is local to that contribute.

## Size and memory

- Snapshots can be **large** (`environment::`, `request::`, nested `qualifiers()` over every active name, multi-entry contribute).
- Prefer everyday **`qualifier::name`**. Do not hold or repeatedly rebuild large snapshots in long-running hosts.
- Another beta pressure point for **#2 / `afw-value-memory`** (pools, managed escape). Maintainer notes: `beta-backlog.md`.

## Model / authoring

- Model `on*` hooks document bags via generate OT **`contextType`** and short property descriptions (`afw-model-adapter`). Optional `qualifier("current")` is debug/tools only.
- **custom::** multi-layer redesign still deferred (residual names under property-level `on*` risk) — see beta-backlog.

## Script-facing: catalogs vs working objects

C may fill a memory object and never `set_immutable`. That is not a script promise.

| Door | Script should see |
|------|-------------------|
| Catalog qualifiers (`environment::`, `process::`, `request::`, `application::`, `adapter::` conf, `custom::` conf) | **Read-only.** SET throws. Do not mint a face over the live catalog. |
| `qualifier()` / `qualifiers()` | **Copy** (#9). Mutating the copy is fine. |
| Retrieve / `get_object` | Working copy (slot fill / view). Local sets; no store write-through. |
| `current::object` | Depends on **which** `current::` frame: model hook ≈ retrieve; auth/index ≈ the resource/row (read). Not “`current::` is always mutable.” |

Live catalog mutation, if ever: a function with execute access and authorization that actually changes the host — not property SET on a wrapper.

## `current::` vs `custom::` (product rule)

| Qualifier | Role |
|-----------|------|
| **`current::`** | Framework **operation context** for this evaluate. **Name set is per context** (auth ≠ model ≠ log ≠ index). |
| **`custom::`** | Conf maintainer **extra variables** for expressions/templates/scripts **within that configured thing**. Compile at conf load when hybrids; evaluate at use. Not a global “every adapter has custom.” |

Push requires a **non-empty** qualifier name (`"Qualifier required"` if empty). Stale docs that mention empty-string qualifier for “unqualified variables” are residual.

## Runtime lookup by name

- Compiled locals: **`symbol_reference`** → frame depth + **index** (not name search).
- Adaptive **`variable_get(name)`** / `variable_exists` / `variable_is_not_null`: optional `qualifier::name`; unqualified uses **by-name** scope walk; qualified uses qualifier stack.
- Index filter/value: use **`current::object`** (or `variable_get("current::object")`), not bare `object` / `variable_get("object")` unless a lexical `object` exists.

Index eval push: **`afw-adapter-index`**.

